course: dictionary
lesson: 8951
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Silver can be a metal, a colour, a second place or things made of silver. «Grandma's best silver spoons come out of the drawer dull and almost black» is about the metal, because spoons are made of silver.
explain: Look at the words around silver. In «Fergus wins a silver medal», silver means second place, not the metal. Mum hugs him, and Dad asks, «Only silver?» That clue tells you silver is good but not the best. Ask yourself: does this fit as a metal, a colour or a place?
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. If you put «a metal» into «a silver medal», it does not make sense, so the meaning must be second place. Checking your meaning like this helps you choose the right one every time.
explain: Silver also appears in sayings, such as «born with a silver spoon in your mouth». A saying does not mean just the words, so the context matters even more. If you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: Silver is a shiny, grey-white precious metal used for jewellery, coins and cutlery.
fact: «Silver» can also mean the shiny grey-white colour, as in a silver car.
fact: «Silver» means second place: a silver medal is won by the runner-up.
fact: Silver conducts electricity very well, so scientists use it when they need electricity to flow easily.
fact: Silver tarnishes: it reacts with sulphur gases in the air and makes a thin black layer, which is why old spoons look dull and almost black.
exercise: «Grandma's best silver spoons come out of the drawer dull and almost black.» In this sentence, what is silver? | *A metal used for spoons | A grey-white colour only | A second place in a race | A kind of jewellery
exercise: «Fergus wins a silver medal.» What does silver mean here? | A silver coin | Gold, the best of all | The colour of the medal | *Second place
exercise: «The lake shone silver in the moonlight.» What does silver mean in this sentence? | Second place in a race | A metal used for spoons | *A shiny grey-white colour
test: «Silver conducts electricity very well.» In science, what does this tell you about silver? | *It lets electricity flow through it easily | It turns electricity into light | It stops electricity completely | It changes colour when electricity flows
test: Why does an old silver spoon look black? | *Silver reacts with sulphur gases in the air and makes a thin black layer | It was left in water for a day | It was painted black by mistake | It is made of a black metal
exam: A book says, «She was born with a silver spoon in her mouth.» What does this saying mean? | She was born on a silver day | She was a very quiet baby | Mum gave her a spoon when she was a baby | *She was born into a rich family
